   "widgets_values": [
    "Read me first\n\nThis is the exact graph that made test plate p-s020 (seed 1370159302). Data flows left to right along the wires; each box does one job. Press Queue (Run) to make the same image again, or change the seed in box 7 for a sibling.\n\nWire colours are types: purple MODEL, yellow CLIP, orange CONDITIONING, pink LATENT, red VAE, blue IMAGE. A wire only connects matching types."
   ],
   "title": "Note",
   "color": "#332922",
   "bgcolor": "#593930"
  },
  {
   "id": 12,
   "type": "Note",
   "pos": [
    40,
    800
   ],
   "size": [
    360,
    250
   ],
   "flags": {},
   "order": 12,
   "mode": 0,
   "inputs": [],
   "outputs": [],
   "properties": {
    "Node name for S&R": "Note"
   },
   "widgets_values": [
    "Boxes 1-2: the model\n\nBox 1 loads Krea 2 Turbo, a 12.9B image model, stored as fp8 (your card upcasts it to bf16). Box 2 adds the LoRA we trained on 40 gallery plates: a small file of weight changes that pulls the model toward her face. Strength 1.0 = full effect; lower it to weaken her face, raise it carefully."
   ],
   "title": "Note",
   "color": "#332922",
   "bgcolor": "#593930"
  },
  {
   "id": 13,
   "type": "Note",
   "pos": [
    1300,
    300
   ],
   "size": [
    360,
    250
   ],
   "flags": {},
   "order": 13,
   "mode": 0,
   "inputs": [],
   "outputs": [],
   "properties": {
    "Node name for S&R": "Note"
   },
   "widgets_values": [
    "Boxes 3-5: the words\n\nBox 3 loads Qwen3-VL-4B, which turns the prompt into numbers the image model understands. Box 4 is the prompt: it starts with the trigger word 'clxudia' (the LoRA learned it), then her fixed features, wardrobe, then the shot. Box 5 makes an empty 'negative' prompt: Turbo is distilled to work without one (CFG 1)."
   ],
   "title": "Note",
   "color": "#332922",
   "bgcolor": "#593930"
  },
  {
   "id": 14,
   "type": "Note",
   "pos": [
    1300,
    620
   ],
   "size": [
    360,
    250
   ],
   "flags": {},
   "order": 14,
   "mode": 0,
   "inputs": [],
   "outputs": [],
   "properties": {
    "Node name for S&R": "Note"
   },
   "widgets_values": [
    "Boxes 6-9: the picture\n\nBox 6 is pure noise at the image size. Box 7 removes noise in 8 steps, steered by the prompt and the model: 'seed' decides the starting noise, so the same seed and prompt give the same image. Box 8-9 convert the result from the model's compressed 'latent' space to real pixels, in tiles so it fits in 16 GB."
   ],
   "title": "Note",
   "color": "#332922",
   "bgcolor": "#593930"
  }
